@startuml
!theme plain
left to right direction
title M4 Profile, Credential, and Extension Boundaries

actor User

package "Containing apps" {
  [ReluxProxyIOS] as IOS
  [ReluxProxyMac] as Mac
  [Profile and Key Repository] as Repo
}

database "App Group Profile Store\nversioned non-secret snapshots\napproved host identities\nopaque Keychain references" as AppGroup
database "Data Protection Keychain\nprivate keys and optional passphrases\nminimum shared access group" as Keychain
component "NETunnelProviderManager\nschema plus opaque profile reference only" as Manager

package "Packet tunnel extensions" {
  [Provider Adapter] as Provider
  [ReluxTunnelCore Runtime] as Runtime
}

node "User-owned SSH host" as Host

User --> IOS : edit profile / manage keys / approve trust
User --> Mac : edit profile / manage keys / approve trust
IOS --> Repo : typed actions
Mac --> Repo : typed actions
Repo --> AppGroup : atomic generation publish
Repo --> Keychain : secret CRUD
IOS --> Manager : select opaque profile generation
Mac --> Manager : select opaque profile generation
Manager --> Provider : start with non-secret reference
Provider --> AppGroup : load immutable generation
Provider --> Keychain : resolve opaque credential after host approval
Provider --> Runtime : compose verified profile and credential
Runtime --> Host : verify host key, then authenticate
Provider --> IOS : versioned status, trust, and diagnostics evidence
Provider --> Mac : versioned status, trust, and diagnostics evidence

note bottom of AppGroup
  Forbidden: raw private keys, passphrases,
  traffic, DNS queries, and destination data
end note

note bottom of Keychain
  Secrets never enter providerConfiguration,
  logs, diagnostics, or board resources
end note

@enduml